[h2]0.8.4[/h2]
[h3]Fisher Flag[/h3]
[list]
[*][b]New Fisher Flag[/b] in the Food menu, right next to the Gatherer Flag. Its fisher catches fresh fish from the shore where the water is clean and deep enough, and shows "Nothing to do in range" where it isn't.
[*]The Gatherer Flag no longer has a "Catch fish" mode. Fresh fish feed the Fish Hatchery, which breeds juvenile fish for the Fishery Works.
[/list]

[h3]Reactor Bots[/h3]
[list]
[*]The Bot Assembler's second recipe is now [b]Reactor bot[/b] and builds Reactor Bots, from a reinforced bot frame, a reactor power cell, four limbs and a head.
[*][b]Reactor Bots stand out:[/b] blackened plating and neon-yellow eyes and joints that glow.
[*]Workplace windows glow [b]neon green[/b] while a Reactor Bot works there.
[*]The Reactor Charging Bay is back in the Science menu, right after the Charging Station.
[/list]

[h3]Radioactive tides on the new-game screen[/h3]
[list]
[*]Easy, Normal and Hard now set the radioactive tides too, and [b]Customize[/b] has rows for them right under the badtide settings: on or off, cycles without a tide, chance and duration.
[*]Existing saves keep their tide settings. The Mod Settings page is gone, and [b]Mod Settings (eMka) is no longer a required mod[/b] for Deep Frontier.
[/list]

[h3]Fixes[/h3]
[list]
[*]Selecting the Bot Assembler no longer freezes the game.
[/list]
